<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hacienda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A hacienda was a large landed estate in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-america">Spanish America</a>, typically producing livestock or crops and relying on dependent or indebted labour. Haciendas became dominant economic and social units in the colonial countryside. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> they were a central feature of colonial society and the rural economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hacienda.jpg" alt="Hacienda" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Eloquent Peasant · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hacienda_Lealtad,_former_coffee_plantation_in_Lares,_Puerto_Rico_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
